# Day 3 Lab Book Entry: Baseline CMC DCM Inversion and Fit-Quality Inspection

**Date:** Saturday 11 July 2026  
**Project:** MSc Thesis Project  
**Stage:** Source reconstruction + DCM fitting  
**Main objective:** Fit and inspect the baseline six-source CMC DCM for the grand-average Standard vs Pitch Deviant auditory MEG response.

---

## 1. Aim of the day

The aim of Day 3 was to perform the first actual baseline Dynamic Causal Model inversion for the MSc thesis analysis.

This baseline model used the verified six-source Phillips-style auditory network prepared on Day 2. No receptor-informed priors were used at this stage. The purpose of this model is to provide the baseline model evidence value against which later receptor-informed CMC DCMs will be compared.

The key question for this stage was:

> Can the standard six-source CMC DCM explain the 20-participant grand-average MEG response to Standard and Pitch Deviant tones?

---

