---

## 11. ERPs mode interpretation

The ERPs mode plot showed observed vs predicted responses across the eight DCM spatial modes.

The model captured the main Standard and Pitch Deviant response profiles. The fit was strongest in modes 1, 3, 5 and 6. Modes 2 and 4 were less exact but still plausible.

The predicted and observed waveforms were broadly aligned in timing, polarity and shape.

Verdict:

```text
ERPs (mode): acceptable
```

---

## 12. ERPs sources interpretation

The ERPs sources plot showed structured source-level responses across:

```text
left A1
right A1
left STG
right STG
left IFG
right IFG
```

Pitch Deviant responses were generally larger than Standard responses, particularly in auditory and inferior frontal sources.

There was no evidence of flat, unstable or explosive source dynamics.

Verdict:

```text
ERPs (sources): acceptable
```

---

## 13. Coupling A interpretation

The Coupling A plot showed the fitted baseline extrinsic connectivity.

The pattern followed the expected auditory hierarchy:

```text
A1 <-> STG <-> IFG
```

The estimates were structured rather than diffuse across all possible connections.

Verdict:

```text
Coupling (A): acceptable
```

---

## 14. Coupling B interpretation

The Coupling B plot showed Pitch Deviant modulation of connectivity relative to Standard.

The model estimated interpretable condition-specific effects, including:

```text
A1 intrinsic modulation
STG/IFG fronto-temporal modulation
left IFG -> left STG modulation
left STG -> left IFG modulation
right STG -> right IFG modulation
```

This suggests that Pitch Deviant responses were associated with changes in auditory cortical dynamics and fronto-temporal coupling.

Verdict:

```text
Coupling (B): acceptable
```

---

## 15. Coupling C interpretation

The Coupling C plot confirmed auditory driving input to bilateral A1 only.

The fitted input strengths were:

| Source | Input strength | Posterior probability |
|---|---:|---:|
| left A1 | 0.74 | 0.99 |
| right A1 | 0.64 | 1.00 |

No direct driving input was estimated for STG or IFG sources.

Verdict:

```text
Coupling (C): good
```

---

## 16. Trial-specific effects interpretation

The trial-specific effects plot showed the estimated connection strengths separately for:

```text
trial 1 = Standard
trial 2 = Pitch Deviant
```

The main pattern was:

```text
A1 intrinsic/self effects were lower for Pitch Deviant.
STG -> A1 backward effects were lower for Pitch Deviant.
A1 -> STG feedforward effects were relatively stable.
STG/IFG fronto-temporal effects were stronger for Pitch Deviant.
```

Verdict:

```text
Trial-specific effects: acceptable
```

---

## 17. Input plot interpretation

The input plot showed a single transient auditory input function peaking shortly after stimulus onset and returning toward zero.

This is appropriate because both Standard and Pitch Deviant trials receive an auditory stimulus. The condition difference is represented by the B matrix rather than by a separate input function.

Verdict:

```text
Input plot: acceptable
```

---

## 18. Response and response image interpretation

The Response and Response image plots showed good agreement between observed adjusted responses and model-predicted responses.

The model captured:

```text
main timing of the evoked responses
amplitude range
larger Pitch Deviant response
channel-time structure
return toward baseline
```

Verdict:

```text
Response plots: acceptable
```

---

## 19. Scalp maps interpretation

The scalp maps showed good agreement between observed and predicted topographies for both Standard and Pitch Deviant conditions across representative time points.

The model reproduced the main spatial polarity patterns and condition-specific differences.

Verdict:

```text
Scalp maps: good
```

---

## 20. Data plot interpretation

The Data plot showed the observed responses used for DCM fitting.

The data contained clear evoked responses in both conditions, with the Pitch Deviant response visibly stronger and more complex than the Standard response.

There was no evidence of a single rogue channel dominating the plot.

Verdict:

```text
Data plot: acceptable
```

